WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.860
Film Courage: What are a few things you do
to try to get people out of their own way?

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:10.250
Larry Wilson: In terms of teaching and writing
and in that regard?

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:20.170
One thing that I love doing when I’m doing
workshops is having like a “free write”

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:29.269
and I will pick something…a topic that has
happened to me that week…or something that

00:00:29.269 --> 00:00:35.500
is making me really happy or really bothering
me in the world (it can be really personal

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:36.500
and all of that).

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:43.440
And I will ask people to write…let’s just
spend the first half-hour of the class just

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:48.160
writing about that.

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:54.960
And that could be “I was on the phone yesterday
and before I knew it, I was saying things

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:59.910
that I really regret and I wish I could take
back.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:04.690
Have you been on the phone and said things
to someone who you really care about that

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:09.250
you really regret that you can’t take back?”

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:11.860
And of course, everyone has.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:20.240
And people will write and I will be ruthlessly
honest with myself and that will give people

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:26.480
permission to be honest with themselves.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:33.140
And some of the most amazing writing I’ve
had come out of my workshops are those “free

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:34.200
writes.”

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:50.340
And writing…there is going to be so much
rejection, indifference…there is going to

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:57.890
be so many people saying “No, other people
do that.

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:00.990
You don’t do that!

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:02.140
Other people make movies.

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:05.170
You don’t make movies.”

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:09.520
I was with a very talented writer/director
on Sunday night.

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:11.980
Who was from Georgia.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:19.310
And when he said to his family he was moving
to New York to make movies he might as well

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:24.980
have been saying ‘I’m going to Mars to
colonize the red…No!

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:26.150
That is what other people do.

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:29.920
A kid from Georgia doesn’t do that.”

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:35.800
And I just try to convince people to just
relax.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:38.120
Oh my gosh, relax!

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:39.170
Just write it.

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:40.800
Don’t worry about it.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.400
Yeah, some people will hate it.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:45.160
Some people will love it.

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:49.880
BEETLE JUICE got a lot of terrible reviews.

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:51.660
They were wrong.

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:58.230
I was told by one of the most prominent executives
in Hollywood I was ruining my career.

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:02.060
He was wrong.

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:04.460
But so what if they’re right?

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:08.780
You’ll do another one.

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:10.390
I love doing “free writes.”

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:13.530
I love saying ‘reveal a little something
about yourself.

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:15.209
This is a safe place.’

00:03:15.209 --> 00:03:21.780
And it’s amazing what comes out if people
give themselves permission to do that.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:28.720
But it’s hardly a perfect process and so
many people will be so afraid of how they’re

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:36.140
going to be judged by words on a computer
screen for Gosh sakes.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:38.310
It’s a screenplay, okay!

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:40.670
It’s an f’n screenplay.

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:42.620
Get over it.

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:47.319
But they will be so afraid of how they will
be judged and they will be judged a failure

00:03:47.319 --> 00:03:50.760
that they will just quit and figure out something
else to do.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:59.069
So I try and I try and I try to just loosen
people up and say “feel free to fail.”

00:03:59.069 --> 00:04:05.531
I started surfing again after 40 years of
not doing it.

00:04:05.531 --> 00:04:09.340
And I was a really good surfer 40 years ago.

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:12.710
And I started again and was I terrible.

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:19.639
I mean everything I thought I knew…I mean
I knew it in principle but I had to learn

00:04:19.639 --> 00:04:21.340
it again.

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:24.330
And then all the sudden I started getting
good again.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:30.930
But it was after a lot of falling off of a
surfboard and embarrassing myself.

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:41.590
But it’s that same thing, you fall off…you
fall off…you fall off..and then you don’t.

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:44.620
And writing is you’re going to write badly…you’re
going to write badly and then you’re going

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:45.250
to write good.

